DoH queries can be sent with curl for testing, passing the DNS message
in the "dns" query parameter, base64url-encoded with the trailing '='
padding removed (RFC 8484).  The message is easiest to build with
dnspython; message id 0 keeps the URL stable and cache-friendly, as
RFC 8484 recommends for GET requests.

For example:

$ python3 -c 'import base64, dns.message
query = dns.message.make_query("example.", "SOA", id=0)
print(base64.urlsafe_b64encode(query.to_wire()).rstrip(b"=").decode())'
AAABAAABAAAAAAAAB2V4YW1wbGUAAAYAAQ

This string can then be passed to curl:

curl "https://<server>/dns-query?dns=AAABAAABAAAAAAAAB2V4YW1wbGUAAAYAAQ"
